Z||000006||Phantom Rage||04-20-2001||02:26 AM||||I think that would be a great Idea, I too have also played with that notion.  280hp is easily attainable with one of those Mini-Mopar motors, and that’s from just factory parts.  You can also easily find parts for it in the junkyard; e.g. (year dependant) forged parts.   The only gripe I ever really had with them was the turbo lag, but like my friend used to say in his Omni GLHS Shelby, “Just don’t get caught with your pants down.” <P>If you think that is a strange swap, I met someone at my local junkyard that put one into his VW Rabbit.  The only problem I remember him saying was that is was having a minor over heating problem.<BR>||||reg||7
